cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code for "A support-cell secretome program in human hippocampal aging
  is directionally reproducible but not gene-specific"
message: >-
  If you use this code or the result tables, please cite both the software
  (this record) and the manuscript it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shimozaki
    given-names: Koji
    affiliation: >-
      Brain Science Research Unit, Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences,
      Nagasaki University, Nagasaki 852-8523, Japan
    email: shimozak@nagasaki-u.ac.jp
license: MIT
keywords:
  - hippocampal aging
  - single-nucleus multiome
  - secretome
  - reanalysis of public data
  - matched-null controls
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Pre-specified reanalysis of public human hippocampal single-nucleus multiome
  data (GSE268609, with GSE278576, GSE299139, GSE186538, GSE199243, GSE264692
  and GSE325391) through a 2,224-gene secretome lens, with donor-level
  statistics, donor-label permutation calibration of the design itself, and
  expression- and effect-matched null controls for every reported claim.
  Includes the pre-specified analysis documents, the result tables underlying
  every number in the manuscript, and pinned software environments.
